{"wiki_catalogs":[{"id":"1e1df421-adb7-4c92-b915-127653b8bb06","repo_id":"1df36caa-a06b-4bbc-be6e-44a66b435e02","name":"Project Overview","description":"project-overview","prompt":"Create comprehensive content for the Luxerion project overview section. Explain the project's purpose as a vanilla web application, its architecture using HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript without external dependencies. Document the separation of concerns pattern with three core files: index.html for structure, style.css for presentation, and script.js for behavior. Include both conceptual overviews for beginners understanding web fundamentals and technical details for experienced developers. Use terminology consistent with vanilla web development. Provide practical examples demonstrating how these three files work together to create interactive web experiences.","progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"index.html,style.css,script.js","gmt_create":"2026-07-26T17:50:18.4404979+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-07-26T17:50:57.655629+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"b16e59f5-5fde-47ea-815f-c46e3a52fe52","repo_id":"1df36caa-a06b-4bbc-be6e-44a66b435e02","name":"Getting Started","description":"getting-started","prompt":"Create comprehensive getting started content for the Luxerion project. Include installation instructions for local development setup, basic usage examples showing how to open and run the application in a web browser, and initial customization steps. Document the minimal requirements (any modern web browser) and explain how to view the page locally by opening index.html. Provide step-by-step guidance for beginners on modifying colors, text content, and basic functionality. Include troubleshooting tips for common issues like file paths and browser compatibility.","order":1,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"index.html,style.css,script.js","gmt_create":"2026-07-26T17:50:18.441166+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-07-26T17:50:48.0857733+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"fea99a39-f1e3-4667-b861-ef7ccd39015e","repo_id":"1df36caa-a06b-4bbc-be6e-44a66b435e02","name":"File Structure and Organization","description":"file-structure","prompt":"Create detailed content for the file structure and organization section. Explain the flat directory structure with three core files and their specific responsibilities. Document how index.html serves as the main entry point containing semantic HTML5 markup, meta tags, and resource linking. Describe style.css as the styling layer handling visual presentation, responsive design, and animations. Detail script.js as the behavioral layer managing DOM manipulation, event handling, and user interactions. Include diagrams showing how these files interact and reference each other through proper linking mechanisms.","order":2,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"index.html,style.css,script.js","gmt_create":"2026-07-26T17:50:18.44183+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-07-26T17:50:51.0023094+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"99688616-8cae-439d-abeb-84a0b754c29e","repo_id":"1df36caa-a06b-4bbc-be6e-44a66b435e02","name":"HTML Structure Documentation","description":"html-documentation","prompt":"Create comprehensive HTML documentation for the index.html file. Document the document hierarchy, semantic HTML5 elements used, meta tags configuration, and SEO considerations. Explain the resource linking strategy for CSS and JavaScript files, viewport settings for responsive design, and accessibility features implemented. Include detailed explanations of each major section within the HTML structure, element relationships, and best practices followed. Provide examples of how to add new sections, modify existing content, and maintain semantic markup standards.","order":3,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"index.html","gmt_create":"2026-07-26T17:50:18.44183+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-07-26T17:51:22.890573+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"24dd3edc-f015-44eb-8495-ae963b440a9c","repo_id":"1df36caa-a06b-4bbc-be6e-44a66b435e02","name":"CSS Styling System","description":"css-styling-system","prompt":"Create detailed CSS documentation for the styling system. Document the color scheme, typography choices, layout patterns, and responsive design implementation. Explain CSS custom properties if used, media queries for different screen sizes, and animation/transition effects. Include guidelines for maintaining consistent styling, adding new components, and overriding default styles. Document browser compatibility considerations, performance optimization techniques, and accessibility features in the CSS implementation. Provide examples of common styling modifications and best practices for extending the visual system.","order":4,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"style.css","gmt_create":"2026-07-26T17:50:18.4427362+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-07-26T17:51:42.414918+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"44a67f40-775f-49fb-8eed-a3ab3e30828a","repo_id":"1df36caa-a06b-4bbc-be6e-44a66b435e02","name":"JavaScript Functionality","description":"javascript-functionality","prompt":"Create comprehensive JavaScript documentation for the interactive functionality. Document DOM manipulation patterns, event handling implementation, and user interaction logic. Explain any data management, state handling, or dynamic content updates. Include detailed explanations of functions, their parameters, return values, and usage patterns. Document performance considerations, browser compatibility, and debugging approaches. Provide examples of extending functionality, adding new events, and integrating with external APIs if applicable. Address common issues and troubleshooting techniques for JavaScript-specific problems.","order":5,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"script.js","gmt_create":"2026-07-26T17:50:18.443911+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-07-26T17:51:31.6628153+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"f2ddd6e8-c605-423d-a410-dc624b8b2a71","repo_id":"1df36caa-a06b-4bbc-be6e-44a66b435e02","name":"Customization Guide","description":"customization-guide","prompt":"Create detailed customization documentation for modifying the Luxerion project. Explain how to change colors, fonts, layouts, and content across all three files. Document the process of adding new sections to the HTML, creating custom CSS styles, and implementing new JavaScript features. Include step-by-step guides for common customizations like changing the theme, adding navigation elements, modifying forms, or integrating third-party libraries. Provide code examples for typical modifications and explain the relationships between HTML structure, CSS styling, and JavaScript behavior when making changes.","order":6,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"index.html,style.css,script.js","gmt_create":"2026-07-26T17:50:18.443911+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-07-26T17:52:26.3236797+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"ba06f15d-a925-40ea-bbdc-b63b7866b028","repo_id":"1df36caa-a06b-4bbc-be6e-44a66b435e02","name":"Deployment Guide","description":"deployment-guide","prompt":"Create comprehensive deployment documentation for the Luxerion project. Document various deployment options including static hosting services (GitHub Pages, Netlify, Vercel), traditional web servers, and local development environments. Explain file preparation, optimization techniques for production, and performance considerations. Include step-by-step deployment instructions for popular platforms, domain configuration, SSL setup, and monitoring. Address caching strategies, asset optimization, and troubleshooting common deployment issues. Provide guidance on version control integration and continuous deployment setup.","order":7,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"index.html,style.css,script.js","gmt_create":"2026-07-26T17:50:18.4445011+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-07-26T17:52:27.5257017+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"}],"wiki_items":[{"catalog_id":"b16e59